<quiz>
  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Compound interest: how much to invest now (INNODEMS)</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>{@nm@} wants to have Ksh \( {@A0@} \) in \( {@T0@} \) years' time to pay for college fees. A savings account pays \( {@R0@}\% \) per annum compound interest, compounded {@freqw@}.</p>
<p>How much must {@nm@} invest now? Give your answer to the nearest shilling.</p>
<div>Amount to invest \( = \) Ksh [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]]</div>
<div>[[feedback:prt1]]</div>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Here the final amount \( A \) is known and the principal \( P \) is unknown. The rate per period is \( \dfrac{ {@R0@} }{ {@kk@} } = {@rd(rp)@}\% \) and there are \( {@kk@} \times {@T0@} = {@nper@} \) periods.</p>
\[
\begin{align*}
{@A0@} &= P\left(1 + \frac{ {@rd(rp)@} }{100}\right)^{ {@nper@} } \\
P &= \frac{ {@A0@} }{ ({@float(1 + rp/100)@})^{ {@nper@} } } = {@round(P0)@}.
\end{align*}
\]
<p>{@nm@} must invest about Ksh \( {@round(P0)@} \) now. Check: \( {@round(P0)@} \times ({@float(1 + rp/100)@})^{ {@nper@} } \approx {@A0@} \).</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
    <defaultgrade>1</defaultgrade>
    <penalty>0.1</penalty>
    <hidden>0</hidden>
    <idnumber/>
    <stackversion>
      <text>2025010100</text>
    </stackversion>
    <questionvariables>
      <text><![CDATA[nm : rand(["Esther", "Kelvin", "Wanjiru", "Otieno", "Achieng", "Kiprono", "Amina", "Mutua"]);
rd(v) := if integerp(v) then v else float(v);
fq : rand([[1, "annually"], [2, "semi-annually"], [4, "quarterly"]]);
kk : fq[1];
freqw : fq[2];
A0 : rand([150000, 200000, 400000, 500000, 750000]);
R0 : rand([6, 8, 10, 12]);
T0 : rand([3, 4, 5, 6, 8]);
rp : R0/kk;
nper : kk*T0;
P0 : A0/(1 + rp/100)^nper;
w_mult  : A0*(1 + rp/100)^nper;          /* multiplied instead of divided */
w_simple: A0/(1 + R0*T0/100);            /* simple interest in reverse */
w_noadj : A0/(1 + R0/100)^T0;            /* did not adjust for the compounding period */]]></text>
    </questionvariables>
